### ==============================================================================
### MASTER HTTP ACCEPTANCE TEST SUITE: OrderService & In-Process Saga Workflow
### Target Service: OrderService (Port 5267:8080, DB: OrderDb)
### Integrated Services: AuthService (Port 5265), CatalogService (Port 5000/5266)
### Coverage: All 23 Features (F-01 -> F-23) & Acceptance Criteria (AC 2.a -> AC 2.k)
### ==============================================================================

@AuthService_Host = http://localhost:5265
@CatalogService_Host = http://localhost:5000
@OrderService_Host = http://localhost:5267
# Trùng với InternalApi:Key của OrderService (để trống ở dev thì header này bị bỏ qua)
@internalApiKey = 

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SECTION 0: AUTHENTICATION & PERSONA TOKEN ACQUISITION (RBAC SETUP)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 0.1 Provision Admin Persona via AuthService
# @name provisionAdmin
POST {{AuthService_Host}}/api/auth/users/provision-staff
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin_e2e@example.com",
  "password": "Admin@123456!",
  "fullName": "System Admin E2E",
  "role": "Admin"
}

### Store Admin Token
@adminToken = {{provisionAdmin.response.body.auth.accessToken}}

### 0.2 Provision LogisticsStaff Persona via AuthService
# @name provisionStaff
POST {{AuthService_Host}}/api/auth/users/provision-staff
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "staff_e2e@example.com",
  "password": "Staff@123456!",
  "fullName": "Logistics Staff E2E",
  "role": "LogisticsStaff"
}

### Store Logistics Staff Token
@staffToken = {{provisionStaff.response.body.auth.accessToken}}

### 0.3 Provision Customer A Persona via AuthService
# @name provisionCustomerA
POST {{AuthService_Host}}/api/auth/users/provision-staff
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer_a@example.com",
  "password": "Customer@123456!",
  "fullName": "Customer A E2E",
  "role": "Customer"
}

### Store Customer A Token & ID
@customerAToken = {{provisionCustomerA.response.body.auth.accessToken}}
@customerAUserId = {{provisionCustomerA.response.body.auth.userId}}

### 0.4 Provision Customer B Persona via AuthService (for Tenant Isolation Tests)
# @name provisionCustomerB
POST {{AuthService_Host}}/api/auth/users/provision-staff
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer_b@example.com",
  "password": "Customer@123456!",
  "fullName": "Customer B E2E",
  "role": "Customer"
}

### Store Customer B Token & ID
@customerBToken = {{provisionCustomerB.response.body.auth.accessToken}}
@customerBUserId = {{provisionCustomerB.response.body.auth.userId}}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SECTION 1: CATALOG SERVICE DISCOVERY & SEED VERIFICATION
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1.1 Discover Active Catalog Products (Ultraboost, Samba, Stan Smith)
# @name getCatalogProducts
GET {{CatalogService_Host}}/api/catalog/products?page=1&pageSize=10
Accept: application/json

### Note Product IDs from Catalog Response:
# Sample Product ID 1 (Ultraboost Light): 6ad318f7691a1e702d881190 (Size: 40, 41, 42 - Price: 3,800,000 VND)
# Sample Product ID 2 (Samba OG):         6ad318f7691a1e702d881191 (Size: 40, 41, 42 - Price: 2,700,000 VND)
@productId1 = 6ad318f7691a1e702d881190
@productId2 = 6ad318f7691a1e702d881191


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SECTION 2: SHOPPING CART DOMAIN OPERATIONS (F-01 to F-05)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2.1 Fetch Empty Cart for Customer A (F-01)
# Expect: 200 OK, items: [], totalItems: 0, subTotal: 0
GET {{OrderService_Host}}/api/carts/my-cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 2.2 Add Item 1 (Size 42, Qty 1) to Customer A's Cart (F-02)
# Expect: 200 OK or 201 Created
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/carts/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "{{productId1}}",
  "productName": "Adidas Ultraboost Light Unisex",
  "size": 42,
  "quantity": 1,
  "unitPrice": 3800000,
  "thumbnailUrl": "https://assets.adidas.com/sample.jpg"
}

### 2.3 Increment Quantity by Adding Same Product & Size (Qty 2) (F-02)
# Expect: 200 OK, item quantity becomes 3
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/carts/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "{{productId1}}",
  "productName": "Adidas Ultraboost Light Unisex",
  "size": 42,
  "quantity": 2,
  "unitPrice": 3800000,
  "thumbnailUrl": "https://assets.adidas.com/sample.jpg"
}

### 2.4 Update Item Quantity Directly to 1 (F-03)
# Expect: 200 OK, item quantity updated to 1
PUT {{OrderService_Host}}/api/carts/items/{{productId1}}/42
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 1
}

### 2.5 Add Second Item (ProductId2, Size 40, Qty 1) (F-02)
# Expect: 200 OK, cart now has 2 distinct line items
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/carts/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "{{productId2}}",
  "productName": "Adidas Samba OG Classic",
  "size": 40,
  "quantity": 1,
  "unitPrice": 2700000,
  "thumbnailUrl": "https://assets.adidas.com/samba.jpg"
}

### 2.6 Remove Item 2 from Cart (F-04)
# Expect: 200 OK, Item 2 removed; Item 1 remains
DELETE {{OrderService_Host}}/api/carts/items/{{productId2}}/40
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}

### 2.7 Clear Cart Completely (F-05)
# Expect: 200 OK, cart emptied
DELETE {{OrderService_Host}}/api/carts/clear
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}

### 2.8 Verify Cart is Empty
# Expect: 200 OK, items: []
GET {{OrderService_Host}}/api/carts/my-cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SECTION 3: ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA VERIFICATION (AC 2.a THROUGH AC 2.k)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### ==============================================================================
### AC 2.a: Valid Checkout with Zero-Trust Pricing Snapshot
### - Client passes fake low price (unitPrice: 1000 VND).
### - Server discards fake price; takes authoritative snapshot from Catalog (3,800,000 VND).
### - Stock reservation created in Catalog with 15m TTL.
### - Order status: AwaitingPayment.
### ==============================================================================

# @name checkoutAc2a
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
X-Idempotency-Key: AC2A-CHECKOUT-001-{{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Nguyen Van A",
  "customerPhone": "0912345678",
  "shippingAddress": {
    "addressLine": "123 Le Loi Street",
    "ward": "Ben Nghe Ward",
    "district": "District 1",
    "city": "Ho Chi Minh City"
  },
  "paymentMethod": "COD",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId1}}",
      "size": 42,
      "quantity": 1,
      "unitPrice": 1000
    }
  ]
}

### Extract Order ID from AC 2.a
@orderIdAc2a = {{checkoutAc2a.response.body.id}}

### Inspect Order Details to Verify Zero-Trust Price Snapshot
# Expect: unitPrice = 3800000, subTotal = 3800000 (fake 1000 VND completely ignored!)
# Expect: orderStatus = "AwaitingPayment"
GET {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/{{orderIdAc2a}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}

### Inspect Catalog Stock Reservation for Order AC 2.a
# Expect: status = "Reserved", holdMinutes = 15
GET {{CatalogService_Host}}/api/catalog/internal/stock/reservations/{{orderIdAc2a}}


### ==============================================================================
### AC 2.b: Checkout Exceeding Catalog Stock -> HTTP 409 Conflict
### - Requested quantity (999) exceeds available inventory.
### - Catalog returns 409 OutOfStock.
### - OrderService propagates 409 Conflict; zero order document created in OrderDb.
### ==============================================================================

POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
X-Idempotency-Key: AC2B-OVERSTOCK-001-{{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Nguyen Van A",
  "customerPhone": "0912345678",
  "shippingAddress": {
    "addressLine": "123 Le Loi Street",
    "ward": "Ben Nghe Ward",
    "district": "District 1",
    "city": "Ho Chi Minh City"
  },
  "paymentMethod": "Online_QR",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId1}}",
      "size": 42,
      "quantity": 999,
      "unitPrice": 3800000
    }
  ]
}
# Expect: HTTP 409 Conflict
# Response body contains: status: "OutOfStock", failedItems list


### ==============================================================================
### AC 2.c: Idempotency Key Replay -> Exactly-Once Order & Reservation
### - Resending identical request with same X-Idempotency-Key returns cached response.
### - No second order document created in Orders collection.
### - Catalog reservation is NOT duplicated.
### ==============================================================================

@idempotencyKeyAc2c = AC2C-IDEMP-KEY-9999

### First Request: Create Order with Unique Idempotency Key
# @name checkoutFirstAttempt
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerBToken}}
X-Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKeyAc2c}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Tran Thi B",
  "customerPhone": "0987654321",
  "shippingAddress": {
    "addressLine": "456 Tran Hung Dao",
    "ward": "Ward 5",
    "district": "District 5",
    "city": "Ho Chi Minh City"
  },
  "paymentMethod": "COD",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId2}}",
      "size": 40,
      "quantity": 1,
      "unitPrice": 2700000
    }
  ]
}
# Expect: HTTP 201 Created

### Extract Order ID from First Attempt
@firstOrderId = {{checkoutFirstAttempt.response.body.id}}

### Second Request: Immediate Replay with Identical Idempotency Key
# @name checkoutReplayAttempt
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerBToken}}
X-Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKeyAc2c}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Tran Thi B",
  "customerPhone": "0987654321",
  "shippingAddress": {
    "addressLine": "456 Tran Hung Dao",
    "ward": "Ward 5",
    "district": "District 5",
    "city": "Ho Chi Minh City"
  },
  "paymentMethod": "COD",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId2}}",
      "size": 40,
      "quantity": 1,
      "unitPrice": 2700000
    }
  ]
}
# Expect: HTTP 201 Created (Cached Replay)
# Response body matches firstOrderId exactly!


### ==============================================================================
### AC 2.d: High-Value Policy (>= 5,000,000 VND)
### - Choosing COD triggers HTTP 400 Bad Request.
### - Choosing Online succeeds with DeliveryOtpCode (6 digits) & SecuritySealCode (SEAL-xxxxxx).
### ==============================================================================

### 1. High-Value with COD -> Expect 400 Bad Request
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
X-Idempotency-Key: AC2D-HIGHVAL-COD-{{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Nguyen Van A",
  "customerPhone": "0912345678",
  "shippingAddress": {
    "addressLine": "123 Le Loi Street",
    "ward": "Ben Nghe Ward",
    "district": "District 1",
    "city": "Ho Chi Minh City"
  },
  "paymentMethod": "COD",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId1}}",
      "size": 42,
      "quantity": 2,
      "unitPrice": 3800000
    }
  ]
}
# Expect: HTTP 400 Bad Request ("Đơn hàng từ 5.000.000 VNĐ bắt buộc thanh toán Online 100%")

### 2. High-Value with Online Payment -> Expect 201 Created with OTP & Security Seal
# @name checkoutHighValueOnline
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
X-Idempotency-Key: AC2D-HIGHVAL-ONLINE-{{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Nguyen Van A",
  "customerPhone": "0912345678",
  "shippingAddress": {
    "addressLine": "123 Le Loi Street",
    "ward": "Ben Nghe Ward",
    "district": "District 1",
    "city": "Ho Chi Minh City"
  },
  "paymentMethod": "Online_QR",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId1}}",
      "size": 42,
      "quantity": 2,
      "unitPrice": 3800000
    }
  ]
}
# Expect: HTTP 201 Created
# Assertions:
# - isHighValue == true
# - deliveryOtpCode matches /^\d{6}$/
# - securitySealCode matches /^SEAL-[A-Z0-9]{6}$/


### ==============================================================================
### AC 2.e: Anti-Hoarding Guard (Chống găm hàng)
### - Maximum 2 active AwaitingPayment orders per user.
### - Attempting a 3rd order triggers HTTP 429 Too Many Requests.
### ==============================================================================

# Note: Customer A currently has 2 active AwaitingPayment orders (from AC 2.a and AC 2.d).
# Attempting a 3rd checkout must be rejected immediately!

POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
X-Idempotency-Key: AC2E-HOARDING-3RD-{{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Nguyen Van A",
  "customerPhone": "0912345678",
  "shippingAddress": {
    "addressLine": "123 Le Loi Street",
    "ward": "Ben Nghe Ward",
    "district": "District 1",
    "city": "Ho Chi Minh City"
  },
  "paymentMethod": "Online_QR",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId2}}",
      "size": 40,
      "quantity": 1,
      "unitPrice": 2700000
    }
  ]
}
# Expect: HTTP 429 Too Many Requests
# Response contains: activeAwaitingOrdersCount = 2


### ==============================================================================
### AC 2.f: Order Cancellation -> Catalog Stock Released & Timeline Updated
### - Customer cancels own AwaitingPayment order.
### - Order status becomes "Cancelled".
### - Catalog reservation moves to "Released".
### - AuditTrail logs cancellation event with actor and timestamp.
### ==============================================================================

### Cancel Customer A's First Order (orderIdAc2a)
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/{{orderIdAc2a}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Khách hàng đổi ý muốn chọn size khác"
}
# Expect: HTTP 200 OK, orderStatus: "Cancelled"

### Verify Catalog Reservation is Released (Stock Restored)
# Expect: status = "Released", releaseReason = "OrderCancelledByUser"
GET {{CatalogService_Host}}/api/catalog/internal/stock/reservations/{{orderIdAc2a}}

### Inspect AuditTrail Timeline for Order AC 2.a
# Expect: 200 OK, timeline has entry with fromState: "AwaitingPayment", toState: "Cancelled"
GET {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/{{orderIdAc2a}}/timeline
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}


### ==============================================================================
### AC 2.g: Order Expiration & Safe Late Payment Rejection
### - Order in AwaitingPayment exceeds 15-minute TTL.
### - Worker transitions order to Expired and releases Catalog stock.
### - Late payment callback arriving after Expired is safely rejected (Stock NOT confirmed).
### ==============================================================================

### Create Order for Expiration Scenario
# @name checkoutForExpiry
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerBToken}}
X-Idempotency-Key: AC2G-EXPIRY-ORDER-{{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Tran Thi B",
  "customerPhone": "0987654321",
  "shippingAddress": {
    "addressLine": "456 Tran Hung Dao",
    "ward": "Ward 5",
    "district": "District 5",
    "city": "Ho Chi Minh City"
  },
  "paymentMethod": "Online_Card",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId2}}",
      "size": 40,
      "quantity": 1,
      "unitPrice": 2700000
    }
  ]
}

@orderIdForExpiry = {{checkoutForExpiry.response.body.id}}

### Simulate/Wait for Saga Timeout Sweep (or trigger cleanup)
# In production, OrderSagaTimeoutWorker sweeps every 15-30s when ExpiresAt < UtcNow.
# Once expired, order moves to "Expired" and Catalog releases stock.

### Send Late Payment Callback for Expired/Cancelled Order
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/internal/payment-callback
X-Internal-Api-Key: {{internalApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "{{orderIdAc2a}}",
  "paymentTransactionId": "TXN-LATE-9999",
  "amount": 3800000,
  "paymentMethod": "Online_QR",
  "callbackTimestamp": "2026-10-19T08:00:00Z"
}
# Expect: Safe Rejection (HTTP 400 Bad Request or 200 with status "LatePaymentDetected" / Auto-Refund flagged)
# Crucial Invariant: Catalog stock MUST NOT be confirmed!

### Verify Catalog Reservation is Still Released (NOT Confirmed)
GET {{CatalogService_Host}}/api/catalog/internal/stock/reservations/{{orderIdAc2a}}
# Expect: status remains "Released", NOT "Confirmed"


### ==============================================================================
### AC 2.h: Valid Payment Callback -> PaymentVerified & Catalog Confirmed
### - Payment callback received on-time while order is AwaitingPayment.
### - Order transitions to PaymentVerified -> ReadyForDispatch.
### - Catalog reservation is Confirmed (permanent stock deduction).
### ==============================================================================

### Send Valid On-Time Payment Callback for Order AC 2.c
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/internal/payment-callback
X-Internal-Api-Key: {{internalApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "{{firstOrderId}}",
  "paymentTransactionId": "TXN-SUCCESS-1001",
  "amount": 2700000,
  "paymentMethod": "Online_Card",
  "callbackTimestamp": "2026-10-19T07:45:00Z"
}
# Expect: HTTP 200 OK, order transitions to PaymentVerified / ReadyForDispatch

### Verify Order Status Updated
GET {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/{{firstOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerBToken}}
# Expect: orderStatus = "PaymentVerified" or "ReadyForDispatch"

### Verify Catalog Reservation Confirmed
GET {{CatalogService_Host}}/api/catalog/internal/stock/reservations/{{firstOrderId}}
# Expect: status = "Confirmed", confirmedAt is NOT null


### ==============================================================================
### AC 2.i: VipBulk Policy & Manual Approval
### - Total >= 15,000,000 VND OR Quantity >= 4 pairs.
### - Flag RequiresManualApproval = true.
### - Customer attempt to approve -> HTTP 403 Forbidden.
### - Admin / LogisticsStaff approve -> HTTP 200 OK, AuditTrail updated.
### ==============================================================================

### Create VipBulk Order (4 Pairs of Ultraboost = 15,200,000 VND)
# @name checkoutVipBulk
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
X-Idempotency-Key: AC2I-VIPBULK-{{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Nguyen Van A VIP",
  "customerPhone": "0912345678",
  "shippingAddress": {
    "addressLine": "123 Le Loi Street",
    "ward": "Ben Nghe Ward",
    "district": "District 1",
    "city": "Ho Chi Minh City"
  },
  "paymentMethod": "Online_QR",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId1}}",
      "size": 42,
      "quantity": 4,
      "unitPrice": 3800000
    }
  ]
}
# Expect: HTTP 201 Created
# Assertions:
# - isHighValue == true
# - isVipBulk == true
# - requiresManualApproval == true
# - isManuallyApproved == false

@vipBulkOrderId = {{checkoutVipBulk.response.body.id}}

### Customer Attempts to Approve Own VipBulk Order -> Expect 403 Forbidden
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/{{vipBulkOrderId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "notes": "Customer tự duyệt đơn của mình"
}
# Expect: HTTP 403 Forbidden

### Admin Approves VipBulk Order -> Expect 200 OK
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/{{vipBulkOrderId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "notes": "Admin verified customer KYC & high-value profile"
}
# Expect: HTTP 200 OK, isManuallyApproved: true, approvedBy: Admin

### Inspect Timeline to Verify Approval Entry
GET {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/{{vipBulkOrderId}}/timeline
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
# Expect: Timeline contains "VipBulkApproved" trigger action by Admin


### ==============================================================================
### AC 2.j: Strict RBAC Enforcement
### - Anonymous call -> 401 Unauthorized.
### - Customer calling Admin-only API (GET /api/orders) -> 403 Forbidden.
### - Customer A attempting to view Customer B's order -> 403 Forbidden / 404 Not Found.
### ==============================================================================

### 1. Anonymous Call to Protected API -> Expect 401 Unauthorized
GET {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/my-orders
# Expect: HTTP 401 Unauthorized

### 2. Customer Calling Admin/Staff Global Orders API -> Expect 403 Forbidden
GET {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
# Expect: HTTP 403 Forbidden

### 3. Admin / Staff Calling Global Orders API -> Expect 200 OK
GET {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
# Expect: HTTP 200 OK with paginated list of all system orders

### 4. Tenant Isolation: Customer A Attempts to View Customer B's Order
GET {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/{{firstOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
# Expect: HTTP 403 Forbidden (or 404 Not Found)


### ==============================================================================
### AC 2.k: Resilient Outbox Compensations (OrderCompensations)
### - Customer cancels order while CatalogService is unreachable.
### - Compensation record is enqueued in OrderCompensations collection.
### - Inspection API displays pending compensations.
### - Compensation worker retry executes release and marks Succeeded.
### ==============================================================================

### Inspect Pending Outbox Compensations
GET {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/internal/compensations
# Expect: HTTP 200 OK with list of pending/processed compensations

### Trigger Immediate Sweep of Order Compensations (Dev/QA Fast Sweep)
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/internal/compensations/trigger
# Expect: HTTP 200 OK with count of compensations processed


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SECTION 4: CONCURRENCY & OCC RACE CONDITION VERIFICATION (AC 3)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### OCC Verification Notes:
# Two simultaneous transitions executed on the exact same OrderId and Version:
# 1. Thread A: POST /api/orders/{id}/cancel
# 2. Thread B: POST /api/orders/internal/payment-callback
# Both filter on: { OrderId: id, Version: 1, CurrentState: "AwaitingPayment" }
# MongoDB FindOneAndUpdateAsync guarantees atomic execution:
# Exactly ONE transition succeeds and increments Version from 1 to 2.
# The second transition matches 0 documents and returns 409 Conflict / safe abort.


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SECTION M4: CHECKOUT + PAYMENT CALLBACK (COD / Online_QR) -> WAYBILL + EMAIL
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### M4.1 Checkout từ giỏ hàng (thêm hàng vào giỏ trước bằng POST /api/carts/items). Email lấy từ JWT, tên từ claim fullName.
# @name checkout
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerPhone": "0912345678",
  "shippingAddress": {
    "addressLine": "12 Nguyen Hue",
    "ward": "Ben Nghe",
    "district": "Quan 1",
    "city": "TP HCM"
  }
}

### M4.2 Checkout mua ngay (bỏ qua giỏ) + ghi đè email/tên người nhận
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Nguyen Van A",
  "customerPhone": "+84912345678",
  "customerEmail": "nhan_hang@example.com",
  "shippingAddress": { "addressLine": "12 Nguyen Hue", "ward": "Ben Nghe", "district": "Quan 1", "city": "TP HCM" },
  "items": [ { "productId": "REPLACE_WITH_PRODUCT_OBJECT_ID", "size": 42, "quantity": 1 } ]
}

### M4.3 Giả lập PaymentService báo COD (hoặc đổi paymentMethod thành Online_QR) -> ReadyForDispatch + sinh WaybillCode + gửi email
POST {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/internal/payment-callback
X-Internal-Api-Key: {{internalApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "{{checkout.response.body.orderId}}",
  "paymentTransactionId": "COD-TEST-0001",
  "amount": {{checkout.response.body.totalAmount}},
  "paymentMethod": "COD"
}

### M4.4 Xem chi tiết đơn: có customerEmail + waybillCode sau khi callback thành công
GET {{OrderService_Host}}/api/orders/{{checkout.response.body.orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerAToken}}
